From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:07:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Don't clip a body whose overflow went to the viewport

Paint already skipped the clip on the root element, whose overflow
applies to the viewport. A body takes the root's place when html is
overflow: visible (CSS Overflow 3 section 3.3), so it must not clip
either: a scroll lock's overflow: hidden on body cut portalled popups
off at the body's height.
---
 src/render.rs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/render.rs b/src/render.rs
index 111309c..5ba4094 100644
--- a/src/render.rs
+++ b/src/render.rs
@@ -359,9 +359,11 @@ impl<'dom, 'a> BlitzDomPainter<'dom, 'a> {
             .and_then(|el| el.text_input_data())
             .is_some();
         // The root element's overflow is propagated to the viewport (which is clipped by the
-        // window/surface bounds), so the root element must not clip its own overflow.
+        // window/surface bounds), so the root element must not clip its own overflow. Nor
+        // must a body whose overflow went to the viewport in the root's place.
         let is_root_element = self.root_element_id == Some(node_id);
         let should_clip = !is_root_element
+            && !self.dom.propagates_overflow_to_viewport(node_id)
             && (is_image
                 || is_sub_doc
                 || is_text_input
